      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $y = x^2 - 2x + 2$ to get $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2x - 2$.",
        "At $x = 2$, gradient is $2$, so tangent is $y = 2x - 2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate the curve equation with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2x - 2$$",
        "Evaluate the gradient at $A(2, 2)$:\n$$\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=2} = 2(2) - 2 = 2$$",
        "Write the equation of the tangent at $A(2, 2)$:\n$$y - 2 = 2(x - 2) \\implies y = 2x - 4 + 2 \\implies y = 2x - 2$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
